    {
      "id": "s02-carrier-equation",
      "intent": "The equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into window tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into F, the dense carrier field. The window operator reads that same field and forms X from it. The equation keeps the carrier visible, so the compact thought process does not replace the spatial field.",
